findings.finding:
Stage raw_act6 deleted RAW_ACT's B.Cu duplicate. Its SE leg (10.0, 90.78)–(12.5, 93.28) had fenced off the north-east part of the BAT_IN_B outline. With the leg gone, BAT_IN_B now fills that area:
- a 24.2 mm² lobe (box x 7.17–13.6, y 82.54–94.4) that holds no BAT_IN pad or via;
- joined to the old fill only along about 2.9 mm south-east of J124.2 (x 10.71–12.1, y 92.19–94.4).

It replaces 27.9 mm² of GND B.Cu (part of the main piece, no via in it). Copper that used to face GND at 0.15 mm now faces battery voltage at the 0.30 mm zone clearance:
- RAW_ACT: C150.1 and via (12.8, 87.0);
- 3V3: via (12.5, 89.2);
- USB_ILIM: R85.1 and its track;
- BUZZ_OUT / BUZZ_G / Q123.3;
- SERVO2_OUT: R151.2 at 0.334 mm;
- ARM1_SENSE: via (14.55, 94.15), 2.15 → 0.65 mm on B.Cu.

The handoff, the raw_act6 docstring, M3_R7 and R7_VALIDATION do not record this change to the BAT_IN_B / GND_B fills.

Electrical effect is small (Inference):
- the lobe carries no current;
- no via lost a pour connection, and no GND pad's return path moved;
- critical reference 0 / 0; DRC passes.

But it adds battery-voltage neighbours whose shorts would:
- bypass the actuator switch (RAW_ACT);
- overvolt 3V3;
- make ARM1_SENSE read 'armed' with the plug out.

